  "guide": {
    "intro": [
      "Vedanta means the end of the Vedas. It is the philosophy drawn from the Upanishads, asking what the self really is and how to be free of suffering.",
      "The best known school is Advaita, non-dual Vedanta. It holds that the true self and ultimate reality are one. Other schools, such as Vishishtadvaita and Dvaita, see more difference."
    ],
